SUMMARY:AI Storm Readiness Summit: Cybersecurity in the AI Era
DESCRIPTION:Cloud Security Alliance Triangle Chapter\n**The storm of vulne
 rability disclosures from Project Glasswing is the first of many large wav
 es of AI-discovered vulnerabilities that may occur in rapid sequence.** Th
 roughout this summit\, attendees will have the opportunity to examine how 
 advances in AI are reshaping the cybersecurity landscape by dramatically i
 ncreasing the likelihood that attackers can discover new vulnerabilities\,
  develop novel exploits\, and execute complex automated attacks at scale. 
 While AI is also accelerating vulnerability remediation and improving soft
 ware quality\, security leaders are facing a growing asymmetry: the inhere
 nt limitations of patching\, operational constraints\, and expanding attac
 k surfaces create a heavier burden for defenders than for attackers. The s
 ession will explore the strategic implications of this shift\, including c
 ompressed timelines between vulnerability discovery and exploitation\, inc
 reased incident frequency\, and the need to reassess traditional risk mode
 ls and security assumptions.\nAttendees will gain practical guidance on bu
 ilding a more resilient\, AI-ready security program capable of operating a
 t machine speed. Topics include modernizing vulnerability management\, str
 engthening foundational security controls such as segmentation\, zero trus
 t\, and phishing-resistant authentication\, accelerating incident response
  through automation\, and leveraging AI-powered agents to improve security
  operations\, code review\, and risk reduction. Designed for CISOs\, secur
 ity executives\, and board-level stakeholders\, the event provides a roadm
 ap for aligning people\, processes\, governance\, and technology to addres
 s the next generation of cyber threats while enabling organizations to sec
 urely capitalize on the business benefits of AI.\n**AGENDA:**\n📍 *8:30 
 AM* – Registration\, Breakfast & Coffee\n🎤 *9:00 AM* – Welcome - Th
 e CSA Summits\, The Paper Series\, Why We’re Here\n\n* Shankar Chebrolu\
 , President CSA Triangle\n* Sounil Yu\, CAIO\, Knostic\n\n🏢 *9:30 AM* 
 – Host Technical Talk: *Red Hat’s Post-Mythos Experience*\n• Jennife
 r Albertson\, Director of Engineering\, Red Hat\n• Vincent Tsugranes\, P
 rincipal Chief Architect\, Red Hat\n⚡ *10:00 AM – Turbo Talks by Pract
 itioners* *(10 minutes each\, including Q&A)*\n• Chuck Kesler\, CISO\, P
 endo\n• Manny Landron\, CISO\, Enact MI\n• Betsy Brady\, CISO\, IBM Cl
 oud\n• David Faraone\, Global VP\, Booz Allen Hamilton\n• Igor Stolbik
 ov\, Chief Security Architect & Distinguished Engineer\, Lenovo\n• Vinay
  Bansal\, CTO & Principal Engineer Cisco\n• Hai Li\, Director of Securit
 y Research\, Cisco\n• Josiah Hagen (COSAI Workstream Lead)\n🍽️ *12:
 00 PM* – Lunch *(provided by CSA Triangle Chapter)*\n🤝 *1:00 PM* – 
 Breakout Sessions\nFacilitated by Sounil Yu\, CAIO\, Knostic & CSA Triangl
 e Board Members\n🛠️ *2:00 PM* – Report-Backs & Live Build Session\n
 Facilitated by Sounil Yu\, CAIO\, Knostic & CSA Triangle Board Members\n
